        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r316446213-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "The holiest shrine of Lord Shiva in Nepal!",
        "text": "\"Pashupatinath Temple\", a Unesco appointed \"World Heritage Site, is an absolurely must see in Kathmandu. As the holiest shrine dedicated to Lord Shiva in Nepal, the main temple is not opened to non-hinduists. Visitors are allowed only in the outer areas. The atmosphere of death is present at almost everywhere. On the \"ghats\" of Bagmati River (a tributary to the Ganges River), cremation rituals are performed continuosly. Ailing hinduists come to die here, living their last days on the temple's premisses. Misteries and faith! Moments of silence, meditation and respect. Be aware of monkeys (they are all over - keep your belongings safely secured, as they are not at all reliable), fake saddhus (the \"ascetic yogis\" always ready for \"paid\" pictures with western tourists) and street vendors (free souvenirs do not exist in anywhere in the world).\n\nI visited Kathmandu last February, nearly two and a half months before the terrible earthquake that devastated Nepal on April 25, 2015. As a Lord Shiva miracle, \"Pashupatinath Temple\" has suffered only minor damages and is normally opened for visitors. Enjoy!",
        "review_tip": null,
