        "title": "Temple Through The Lens",
        "text": "Apart from religious value, If you're a photographer then this might be your spot. You can take slow shutter snaps of pigeons, different geometrical structure all around the temple, different types of people with different color can give you better portrait too, blur/movement images also comparatively easier to get here. And yes, there's monkeys too! \n\nJust be aware as there are many clever guys roaming around who can impose you to buy something, talks with you nicely, give something like gift then demands for money, offers sight seeing guidance and may ask higher price. Sorry to say, I got this situation in a hot and full of crowd day. I dodged, bet you can too. ;-) ",
