        "title": "Best place for walking at night time",
        "text": "Most quite, calm and high energy place which I ever visit. All time when I'm in Nepal I'm going to that temple... Just to think, relax... may be kind of meditate... There two parts which is divide by Bagamati river. One part where is Shiva Temple - if you are not hindu, you anyway can't go inside, and place for cremation... where is very hard to be. And another part with stupas. Bright side. It's like hell and paradise... Full power!\nI can recommend to go there at night with many reasons: 1. There no people, no tourists, no sellers, no fake-sadhu. Just almost nobody. Dogs, monkeys and may some cremations... You can seat and think about eternally. 2. At night time visit of Pashupatinath is free ))\nEnjoy!",
