        "title": "Our Family visit to Pasuphathinath Temple",
        "text": "Pashupatinath temple is very famous among Hindus, where Hindus come and working Shiva in Pashupatinath temple.  Behind the temple where you can see Bagmathi River and where before burning the bodies, the dead person is dipped in the river then taken cremation. During Monday's a big ceremony done behind the temple where various priests handle lights in various styles.  It is worth watching.\nInside the temple, watch out the monkeys.  While we were there, we watched a monkey snatching a women's purse and taking out the phone and dropping others on the floor and climbing on top and holding the phone on the mouth and trying to catch things thrown by others expecting the monkey to drop the phone.  People making calls to the same phone and the phone ringing, but the same money did not even drop the phone.  So, be careful with your belongings.",
