      {
        "review_id": 310867757,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r310867757-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "For the Devotees!",
        "text": "This Temple holds a special place for its religious value for all Hindus. The temple is situated just 5-6 km from Kathmandu airport and is a part of a modest compound. You can easily walk down thru the lanes to reach the main temple witnessing the last rites and rituals being performed across the river running beside the temple.\nWe went to this place in December of 2014 and it was a nice sunny day.The temple compound is well manged and clean. There are a lot of monkeys (really a lot many!) inside the main temple area... but they do no harm...:)\nYou can hire a temple guide who explains the history and significance of this place and the rituals.... the one we found was quite reasonable and  we felt much more aware and contended after he showed us around the temple.\nOverall we had very good Darshan and felt accomplished! ",
