        "title": "Beautiful Religious & Historical Site",
        "text": "Beautiful temples and old temple grounds. Main temple cannot be entered by non-Hindus. The remaining areas were filled with history and culture, everything was outdoors. There are many smaller temples to see and live Hindu cremations were going on while I was there near the stream/river. There are Sadhu's (Hindu holy men) asking for donations to cleanse your spirit and other Sadhu-types offering astrological charts or readings for a fee. There are monkeys roaming around and a lot of tourists and religious visitors. It was worth the trip to see it all.",
